python3 /home/claude/build.py
## 🏷️ UI Enhancement: Relocate Language Switcher to Bottom Left (Mobile View)

### 📝 Description
We need to improve the mobile user experience by repositioning the language switcher (`BG` / `EN` buttons) from the top header overlay to a fixed/sticky position in the bottom left corner of the viewport, matching our updated design specifications. 

### 📸 Visual Reference
* **Current Implementation:** Language buttons sit at the top right, clashing with the header text/navigation overlay.
* **Target Design:** Move buttons to the bottom left with a clean label: `Language Select: BG / EN`.

---

### 🛠️ Technical Requirements & Implementation Steps

1. **Component Restructuring:**
   * Relocate the Language Switcher component from the top navigation/header container to the main layout wrapper or fixed overlay container.
   
2. **Styling & Positioning (CSS/Tailwind):**
   * Apply fixed positioning to ensure it stays anchored at the bottom left of the mobile viewport.
   * **Target CSS Properties:**
     ```css
     .language-switcher-container {
       position: fixed;
       bottom: 24px; /* Adjust spacing according to grid */
       left: 16px;
       display: flex;
       align-items: center;
       gap: 12px;
       z-index: 50; /* Ensure it stays above background elements but below modals */
     }
     ```

3. **UI Enhancements:**
   * Retain the existing pill-button styles for **BG** (active/gold background) and **EN** (inactive/dark transparent background).
   * Add a text label to the right of the buttons reading: `"Language Select: BG / EN"` in a subtle, readable font color (e.g., light gray/off-white) to match the elegant aesthetic.

4. **Responsive Behavior:**
   * This layout change should specifically target mobile and tablet breakpoints. Ensure it does not break or overlap with desktop navigation layouts.

---

### ✅ Acceptance Criteria
* [ ] Language switcher buttons are successfully moved to the bottom-left corner on mobile devices.
* [ ] The text "Language Select: BG / EN" is visible next to the selectors.
* [ ] Buttons remain fully functional and toggle languages correctly upon tapping.
* [ ] The switcher has proper `z-index` configuration so it doesn't get cut off by background sections or float uncomfortably over primary text.

/* FORCE SWITCH TO BOTTOM LEFT */
[class*="lang"], [class*="Language"] {
  position: fixed !important;
  bottom: 24px !important;
  top: auto !important;
  left: 24px !important;
  right: auto !important;
  display: flex !important;
  align-items: center !important;
  z-index: 99999 !important;
}

[class*="lang"]::after, [class*="Language"]::after {
  content: "Language Select: BG / EN";
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);
  font-size: 13px;
  font-family: sans-serif;
  margin-left: 12px;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
